  {
   "id": "vCuR0va3h2YJ",
   "from": "Markian Pahuta",
   "author": "89a4640ddc6e46d0",
   "date": "2013-08-09T00:08:58Z",
   "subject": "Vectorization of Mulivariate Normal",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Everyone,<div><br></div><div>I went through the user manual and mailing lists, and haven&#39;t seen this done... but just wanted to check.</div><div><br></div><div>The following works:</div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"></blockquote><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multi_normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>This does not:</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multi_normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div></code></div><br></div><div>Are there any ways around this?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div><br></div><div>Mark</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Lw2kv7foXoUJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2013-08-09T00:23:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Vectorization of Mulivariate Normal",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Thursday, August 8, 2013 8:08:58 PM UTC-4, Markian Pahuta wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>I went through the user manual and mailing lists, and haven&#39;t seen this done... but just wanted to check.</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>That is the expected, albeit poor, behavior.<br> </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The following works:</div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"></blockquote><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multi_normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>It would be much better to invert Sigma once before the loop starts and then use multi_normal_prec, like<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_inv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_inv</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mdivide_left_tri_low</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Eye</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multi_normal_prec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Sigma_inv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>where Eye is defined as an identity matrix in the transformed data block.<br> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This does not:</div></div></blockquote><div><br>Correct.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "soyMSBRcJB8J",
